        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "NaOH (0.1 g, 2.50 mmol) was dissolved in methanol (10 mL) and added in a single portion to a methanol solution (10 mL) of 2-acetylcyclopentanone (Haccp, 3; 0.27 mL, 2.27 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 30 min at ambient temperature. [Y(NO3)3·6H2O] (1; 0.28 g, 0.75 mmol) dissolved in methanol (10 mL) and water (5 mL) was added dropwise, and stirring was continued for 1 h. The solution volume was reduced by half, water (25 mL) was added, and the precipitate was filtered off, washed with water (30 mL), and dried in vacuum. Colorless crystals of 4 suitable for X-ray diffraction were obtained by slow evaporation of a diethyl ether solution at ambient temperature.",
